1r98|n|A riddle or sieve. ; The mechanical appliance by means of which a vessel is guided or steered when in motion. It is a broad and flat blade made of wood or iron, with a long shank, and is fastened in an upright position, usually by one edge, to the sternpost of the vessel in such a way that it can be turned from side to side in the water by means of a tiller, wheel, or other attachment. ; Fig.: That which resembles a rudder as a guide or governor; that which guides or governs the course.	a:1b4z,70,4;fup,66,4;9u,60,3;ujc,56,6;q0o,51,12;1q0c,51,2;ffm,51,11;g88,51,3;1e88,51,26;ifj,50,2;fkt,48,4;14i,44,3;1vch,43,3;1274,41,5;1z59,37,4~1e88,51,26;1qmx,0,21;tml,3,12;q0o,51,12;ffm,51,11;17zj,20,10;274e,27,8;1593,3,7;f3j,19,6;ujc,56,6;zw,2,6;7mq,20,5;1274,41,5;45o,12,5;1khj,18,5	v:1cdl,87,4;fkw,76,3;ifj,75,11;432,42,48;i87,34,2;433,28,7;10b3,24,1;14h,17,3;42t,13,3;shd,12,4;10ti,11,2;10av,11,1;1osy,11,1;16mq,10,2;1b59,8,5~26eh,5,61;432,42,48;15n8,7,13;ifj,75,11;a7s,1,7;433,28,7;1pr6,6,6;1b59,8,5;1tlb,1,4;1cdl,87,4;shd,12,4;42t,13,3;14h,17,3;fkw,76,3;10ti,11,2	V:12ev,95,7;13m7,68,5;ifj,60,4;bh1,46,4;116f,27,3;2333,26,2;42t,23,6;vt,21,2;6q9,20,4;130g,16,4;1osy,11,1;e6b,6,2;1pr7,4,5;1ltg,3,2;167n,0,2~12ev,95,7;42t,23,6;13m7,68,5;1pr7,4,5;ifj,60,4;bh1,46,4;6q9,20,4;130g,16,4;116f,27,3;2333,26,2;vt,21,2;1ltg,3,2;167n,0,2;e6b,6,2;1osy,11,1	n:hox,59,4;ngi,57,13;1r98,39,6;q0n,33,3;1wxw,28,7;1osr,26,8;1e88,20,3;29js,13,1;267e,12,3;20kj,10,3;m4o,10,5;tgm,9,5;1ixs,8,4;s81,3,6;1td,2,6~ngi,57,13;1osr,26,8;1wxw,28,7;s81,3,6;1r98,39,6;1td,2,6;m4o,10,5;tgm,9,5;hox,59,4;1ixs,8,4;q0n,33,3;267e,12,3;20kj,10,3;1e88,20,3;29js,13,1	N:ifl,99,208;lzx,97,4;n3q,83,19;5l1,77,108;fkx,67,6;xe,64,5;l4f,62,6;1q9b,61,5;81e,60,4;xxp,60,6;ngi,55,11;16aq,51,3;sgi,47,2;cg9,44,5;1b56,42,14~ifl,99,208;5l1,77,108;1le1,35,47;n3q,83,19;42p,8,17;23e9,39,15;1b56,42,14;fdl,5,12;23ql,40,11;ngi,55,11;qvo,20,9;26eb,10,6;xxp,60,6;fkx,67,6;l4f,62,6
