1rdb|a|Moving or advancing by running. ; Having a running gait; not a trotter or pacer. ; trained and kept for running races; as, a running horse. ; Successive; one following the other without break or intervention; -- said of periods of time; as, to be away two days running; to sow land two years running. ; Flowing; easy; cursive; as, a running hand. ; Continuous; keeping along step by step; as, he stated the facts with a running explanation. ; Extending by a slender climbing or trailing stem; as, a running vine. ; Discharging pus; as, a running sore.	j:18bq,39,2;tw9,33,7;1fh9,29,1;1k1,27,4;1hh5,25,2;1q0z,21,5;22b8,17,2;gdc,17,5;v3q,16,3;1tow,13,1;hev,11,5;546,10,5;1ck9,10,2;w01,9,3;wys,8,3~tw9,33,7;22aw,5,6;13vt,2,6;1uby,8,6;1696,0,6;147k,4,5;gdc,17,5;1q0z,21,5;hev,11,5;546,10,5;1k1,27,4;uss,7,4;13q8,2,4;e1j,7,4;u05,8,3	e:ek3,7,3;1xbi,4,1;o60,1,2~ek3,7,3;o60,1,2;1xbi,4,1
