1rdr|n|The act of breaking apart, or separating; the state of being broken asunder; as, the rupture of the skin; the rupture of a vessel or fiber; the rupture of a lutestring. ; Breach of peace or concord between individuals; open hostility or war between nations; interruption of friendly relations; as, the parties came to a rupture. ; Hernia. See Hernia. ; A bursting open, as of a steam boiler, in a less sudden manner than by explosion. See Explosion.	a:u8z,120,3;9gj,88,3;18ui,60,1;244v,60,4~244v,60,4;u8z,120,3;9gj,88,3;18ui,60,1	n:20ps,80,3;18ui,76,3;1695,23,3;kyx,17,2~1695,23,3;18ui,76,3;20ps,80,3;kyx,17,2
