1re9|n|A name given to many aquatic or marsh-growing endogenous plants with soft, slender stems, as the species of Juncus and Scirpus. ; The merest trifle; a straw. ; A moving forward with rapidity and force or eagerness; a violent motion or course; as, a rush of troops; a rush of winds; a rush of water. ; Great activity with pressure; as, a rush of business. ; A perfect recitation. ; A rusher; as, the center rush, whose place is in the center of the rush line; the end rush. ; The act of running with the ball.	a:17d3,79,5;1z59,69,6;1dti,53,5;ynt,44,6;11r2,31,3;170,26,1;7md,25,5;ud5,23,2;1oab,22,4~1z59,69,6;ynt,44,6;17d3,79,5;1dti,53,5;7md,25,5;1oab,22,4;11r2,31,3;ud5,23,2;170,26,1	v:ud5,13,1~ud5,13,1	n:y5m,74,2;1axq,58,4;vbe,45,1;x0g,32,3;1dti,30,1;285t,28,3;170,26,1;1td,22,4;vyy,15,1~1axq,58,4;1td,22,4;x0g,32,3;285t,28,3;y5m,74,2;vbe,45,1;170,26,1;1dti,30,1;vyy,15,1
